Git:
Git is a version control tool used to track and manage changes in your code or project.

GitHub:
GitHub is an online platform used to store, share, and collaborate on Git repositories.

🔗 Relationship

Git manages your project → GitHub stores and shares it online.

Example:

Your Computer
     ↓
    Git
     ↓
   GitHub
     ↓
Online Repository

Easy to remember:
🛠️ Git = Version Control Tool
☁️ GitHub = Online Code Hosting Platform

